Hi, everyone.

It seems that installing the latest version of Zelig (3.0) solves this
problem.  We've just released it to Gary's website, so if you have a
PC or a linux box, start R and type:
   install.packages("Zelig", repos = "http://gking.harvard.edu")
For MacOSX users, the binary should be available on CRAN in a few
days; alternatively, you can download the tar-ball at
http://gking.harvard.edu/src/contrib/Zelig_3.0.tar.gz and install it
at the terminal prompt using R CMD INSTALL Zelig.

Please keep sending bugs in, we appreciate the extra eyes.

Yours,
Olivia

